    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff, mini.sessions\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.x\n\n### Description\n\nI have a function in my config to switch between mini.sessions sessions.:\n\n```lua\n      -- Save old session if active\n      if vim.v.this_session ~= \"\" then\n        MiniSessions.write(nil, {force = true, verbose = false})\n      end\n      -- Open new session\n      MiniSessions.read(item)\n      vim.cmd.clearjumps()\n```\n\nWhen I execute this I sometimes get the following message:\n\n```\nError executing vim.schedule lua callback: (mini.diff) `buf_id` should be `nil` or valid buffer id.\nstack traceback:\n\t[C]: in function 'error'\n\t...AppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/diff.lua:1782: in function 'error'\n\t...AppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/diff.lua:1053: in function 'validate_buf_id'\n\t...AppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/diff.lua:494: in function 'disable'\n\t...AppData/Local/nvim-data/lazy/mini.nvim/lua/mini/diff.lua:1623: in function 'fn'\n\tvim/_editor.lua:351: in function <vim/_editor.lua:350>\n```\n\nI suspect this is because mini.diff is doing its work asynchronously and doesn't like when the buffer is wiped when it is done with its work.\nWould you accept a pull request silencing this error and just silently stop doing work when the buffer is no longer existing?\n\n### Reproduction\n\nHard to reproduce reliable.\n\nOne needs to wipe a buffer while mini.diff is working on it.",
